{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And it came to pass in the first month, on the first day of the month.</b> According to the opinion of our Sages, Scripture mentions that the Tabernacle was set up to stand on the first day of the first month, as He commanded (Exodus 40:2). And it says, \"And Moses set up the Tabernacle\" (Exodus 40:18), to recount what he did when he set it up, beginning from the first day on which he started, which was the twenty-third of Adar. And it does not mention here the anointing of the Tabernacle and its vessels, nor the anointing of Aaron and his sons and the offerings of inauguration, for he did not perform them until he completed the entire erection and was commanded concerning them a second time, \"Take Aaron,\" as is explicit in the portion of צו (Leviticus 8:2). Now the Tabernacle and its vessels were not sanctified for service except through anointing, as it is stated (Exodus 40:9), \"And you shall anoint the Tabernacle and all that is in it, and you shall sanctify it and all its vessels.\" Therefore the meaning of \"and he arranged upon it the arrangement of bread\" (Exodus 40:23), \"and he lit its lamps\" (Exodus 40:25), is that he did so at their proper time after the anointing, and behold they are stated as the reason to do so. And what it also said above (Exodus 40:4), \"and you shall bring in the table and arrange its arrangement,\" is a command that he should arrange it after the anointing. And likewise it said, \"and you shall place the golden altar for incense\" (Exodus 40:5), and likewise \"and he offered upon it the burnt offering and the meal offering\" (Exodus 40:29) — at their proper time, for he had not yet set up the court around the Tabernacle, and one may not offer without hangings, for they would be slaughterers outside; rather, all of them were done at their proper time:"], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:22:44.929944524Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}